-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/12 (19.8.2024), תגמול עובדי הוראה בגין הישגי בית
-- הספר לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ד
-- The one-time grant for the achievements of upper-secondary schools in
-- התשפ"ד, under §36 of the collective agreement of 14.8.2011: who is
-- entitled, the amount by the school's ranking, pro-rating, when it is
-- paid, what it is excluded from and the pension provisions on it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time for the payment duty is counted in SALARY MONTHS from July 2024's
-- (0): August 2024's salary is 1, September 2024's is 2.
`August 2024's salary`    MEANS 1
`September 2024's salary` MEANS 2

DECLARE `school ranking` IS ONE OF
    `top 10%`
    `next 10% (grade 2)`
    `next 10% (grade 3)`
    `next 10% (grade 4)`
    `not ranked`

DECLARE `grant row` HAS
    `ranking` IS A `school ranking`
    `full-position grant` IS A NUMBER

-- What the employer (and, for the reimbursement, the Ministry) does.
DECLARE `grant action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the grant` HAS `grant paid` IS A NUMBER
    `make the pension provisions` HAS `employer part` IS A NUMBER
                                      `employee part` IS A NUMBER
    `make a training-fund provision for the grant`
    `pay the reimbursement` HAS `subject` IS A NUMBER

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/12 — תגמול עובדי הוראה בגין הישגי בית הספר לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ד`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference number, addressees (the owners of educational institutions), greeting, subject line, the recital of the collective agreement of 14.8.2011 with the upper-secondary teachers' union and what it contains, and the circular's purpose (grants for התשפ"ד under §36 of that agreement); no rule.

§§ `1 תחולה`

@desc A teaching employee's school year התשפ"ד in an upper-secondary school, as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `upper-secondary year` HAS
    `graded on the teaching employees' scale in upper-secondary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc graded on the teaching employees' grading and employed in the upper division (חטיבה עליונה)
    `employed by a supervised owner of post-primary education`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed by an owner of post-primary education the Ministry of Education supervises
    `school ranking`                     IS A `school ranking` @desc the school's ranking in the Ministry's examination of achievements (the list of winning schools, section 3)
    `upper-secondary position fraction`  IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position in the upper division (1 = full)
    `share of the year employed at the school` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of התשפ"ד the employee was employed at the excelling school, a maternity-leave period under the Women's Employment Law counting as employed
    `on full sabbatical or unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc on sabbatical or unpaid leave for the whole of התשפ"ד

-- Section 1: every employee graded on the teaching scale in an upper
-- division, employed by a supervised owner of post-primary education, in
-- the Oz LaTmura reform or not yet in it — by the part of the employment in
-- the upper division. "המורים" of section 2 is read as these employees.
@ref akn:art_1/p1
GIVEN y IS AN `upper-secondary year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular applies to` y IF
        y's `graded on the teaching employees' scale in upper-secondary`
    AND y's `employed by a supervised owner of post-primary education`

§§ `2 תגמול עובדי הוראה בגין הישגי בית הספר`

-- 2א: the programme rewarding achievements (scholastic, social and of
-- values) in the upper divisions (grades 9–12/14 in a four-year school,
-- 10–12/14 in a three- or six-year one) has run since התשע"ג by the format
-- and rules of the pedagogical administration's letter of 21.10.2012 — an
-- input: the circular does not restate them.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
ASSUME `the rules of the letter of 21.10.2012` IS A STRING
@desc The format and rules of the achievement-reward programme, set in the letter of 21.10.2012 of the then head of the pedagogical administration; not restated in the circular.

-- 2ב: the one-time grant for a full position, updated to May 2024 by the
-- consumer price index (May 2024 against May 2023), by the school's
-- ranking (printed as lines, not as a table).
@ref akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_b/p2 akn:art_2__para_b/p3 akn:art_2__para_b/p4 akn:art_2__para_b/p5 akn:art_2__para_b/p6 akn:art_2__para_b/p7 akn:art_2__para_b/p8 akn:art_2__para_b/p9 akn:art_2__para_b/p10 akn:art_2__para_b/p11 akn:art_2__para_b/p12
`the grant table` MEANS
    LIST `grant row` `top 10%`            9453.28,
         `grant row` `next 10% (grade 2)` 7089.96,
         `grant row` `next 10% (grade 3)` 4726.65,
         `grant row` `next 10% (grade 4)` 3544.97

GIVEN r IS A `school ranking`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position grant for` r IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD row's `ranking` EQUALS r) `the grant table`
    WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN row's `full-position grant`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- Each ranking has one row, and the grant falls with the ranking.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD count (filter (GIVEN row YIELD row's `ranking` EQUALS r) `the grant table`) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST `top 10%`, `next 10% (grade 2)`, `next 10% (grade 3)`, `next 10% (grade 4)`)
`the grant falls with the ranking` MEANS
        `the full-position grant for` `top 10%` GREATER THAN `the full-position grant for` `next 10% (grade 2)`
    AND `the full-position grant for` `next 10% (grade 2)` GREATER THAN `the full-position grant for` `next 10% (grade 3)`
    AND `the full-position grant for` `next 10% (grade 3)` GREATER THAN `the full-position grant for` `next 10% (grade 4)`
#ASSERT `the grant falls with the ranking`

-- 2ג: part-time and/or part of the year (unpaid leave or sabbatical for
-- part of it included; a maternity-leave period excepted) — the
-- proportional part, by the position in the upper division and/or the part
-- of the year at the excelling school. Its second paragraph: a teacher on
-- full sabbatical or unpaid leave for the year is not entitled.
-- 2ד: employment above 100% is not counted.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c akn:art_2__para_c/p2 akn:art_2__para_d
GIVEN y IS AN `upper-secondary year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of the grant` y IS
    IF y's `on full sabbatical or unpaid leave`
    THEN 0
    ELSE min 1 (y's `upper-secondary position fraction`)
         TIMES min 1 (y's `share of the year employed at the school`)

@ref akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_c
GIVEN y IS AN `upper-secondary year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the achievement grant` y IS
    IF `the circular applies to` y
    THEN `the full-position grant for` (y's `school ranking`) TIMES `the share of the grant` y
    ELSE 0

-- 2ו: the grants are not in the base for the hourly value, severance pay
-- or percentage supplements, and no training-fund provisions are made for
-- them (the training fund is the prohibition below). 2ז: pension
-- provident-fund provisions are made on them — 5% by the employer and 5%
-- deducted from the teacher's salary.
@ref akn:art_2__para_f
GIVEN `base component` IS A STRING @desc a computation the grant could be in the base of, e.g. "hourly value"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grants are left out of the base for` `base component` IF
    elem `base component` (LIST "hourly value", "severance pay", "percentage supplements")

@ref akn:art_2__para_g
`the employer's pension provision rate` MEANS 0.05
@ref akn:art_2__para_g
`the employee's pension deduction rate` MEANS 0.05

-- 2ה: paid in August 2024's salary, and no later than September 2024's.
@ref akn:art_2__para_e
GIVEN y IS AN `upper-secondary year`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grant action`
DECIDE `the grant is paid by September 2024` y IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the grant` g PROVIDED g EQUALS `the achievement grant` y
    WITHIN `September 2024's salary`
    HENCE `the pension provisions on the grant` y
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 2ה: the grant is paid in August 2024's salary and no later than September 2024's"

@ref akn:art_2__para_g
GIVEN y IS AN `upper-secondary year`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grant action`
DECIDE `the pension provisions on the grant` y IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `make the pension provisions` er ee
          PROVIDED er EQUALS `the achievement grant` y TIMES `the employer's pension provision rate`
               AND ee EQUALS `the achievement grant` y TIMES `the employee's pension deduction rate`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 2ז: 5% employer provision and 5% employee deduction to a pension provident fund"

@ref akn:art_2__para_f
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grant action`
DECIDE `no training-fund provision for the grant` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `make a training-fund provision for the grant`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 2ו: no training-fund provisions are made for the grants"

§§ `3–4`

-- Section 3: links to the post-primary division's page on the programme and
-- to the list of winning schools (zochim_2024.pdf). The list decides each
-- school's ranking, which is an input of every employee's year.
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3/p2
ASSUME `the list of winning schools` IS A LIST OF STRING
@desc The winning schools of התשפ"ד (zochim_2024.pdf), linked from section 3; not restated in the circular.

-- Section 4: the owners are reimbursed in the payment system, subject 583,
-- in August 2024's payments transferred to them at the start of 9/2024.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grant action`
DECIDE `the owners are reimbursed` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `pay the reimbursement` s PROVIDED s EQUALS 583
    WITHIN `September 2024's salary`
    LEST BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "section 4: reimbursement under subject 583 in August's payments, transferred at the start of 9/2024"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: the signatures and the copies list; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples, on the circular's own amounts.
`a full-time teacher at a top school` MEANS
    `upper-secondary year` WITH
        `graded on the teaching employees' scale in upper-secondary` IS TRUE
        `employed by a supervised owner of post-primary education`  IS TRUE
        `school ranking`                           IS `top 10%`
        `upper-secondary position fraction`        IS 1.3
        `share of the year employed at the school` IS 1
        `on full sabbatical or unpaid leave`       IS FALSE

`a half-time teacher at a grade-3 school for half the year` MEANS
    `upper-secondary year` WITH
        `graded on the teaching employees' scale in upper-secondary` IS TRUE
        `employed by a supervised owner of post-primary education`  IS TRUE
        `school ranking`                           IS `next 10% (grade 3)`
        `upper-secondary position fraction`        IS 0.5
        `share of the year employed at the school` IS 0.5
        `on full sabbatical or unpaid leave`       IS FALSE

`a teacher on sabbatical all year` MEANS
    `upper-secondary year` WITH
        `graded on the teaching employees' scale in upper-secondary` IS TRUE
        `employed by a supervised owner of post-primary education`  IS TRUE
        `school ranking`                           IS `top 10%`
        `upper-secondary position fraction`        IS 1
        `share of the year employed at the school` IS 1
        `on full sabbatical or unpaid leave`       IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the achievement grant` `a full-time teacher at a top school` EQUALS 9453.28
#ASSERT `the achievement grant` `a half-time teacher at a grade-3 school for half the year` EQUALS 4726.65 TIMES 0.25
#ASSERT `the achievement grant` `a teacher on sabbatical all year` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the grants are left out of the base for` "severance pay"
-- (This asserted the grant IS in the base for "pension", which 2ו does not
-- say: it names only what the grants are left out of.)
#ASSERT NOT `the grants are left out of the base for` "pension"

#TRACE `the grant is paid by September 2024` `a full-time teacher at a top school` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the grant` 9453.28 AT 1
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `make the pension provisions` 472.664 472.664 AT 1
#TRACE `the owners are reimbursed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `pay the reimbursement` 583 AT 2
